Tier 3 suppliers and below","Women
Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"This year we advanced our partnership with the Slave Free Alliance by completing a baseline gap analysis, which covered internal and external aspects of modern slavery, human rights and force labour by conducting interviews with internal employees at all levels and reviewing all our policies and procedure documents.  SFA have now delivered back the findings which will prioritise our improvement activities in this area going forward.","Upskilling our supply chain partners knowledge and understanding of Modern Slavery, Forced Labour and Human Rights.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,"Women
Migrants
Refugees",,United Kingdom,"Together with the United Nations Global Compact (UNGC) UK Network, we successfully completed a second consecutive year of the Sustainable Supplier Training programme. The programme delivered over 6 months included training via online content sessions with associated assessment quizzes and live webinars from both Stagecoach and the UNGC.",Enhancing our tender process due diligence specifically for sourcing our driver uniforms.,Within your supply chains,"Tier 1 suppliers
