China
Hungary
Malaysia","TfL is a member of Electronics Watch, and works with the organisation to address the human and labour rights risks in the ICT supply chains. They managed to improve working hours in Hungary. and aid in resolving other cases. We intervene and use our leverage when there are indications that our suppliers are not using their own leverage to the extent they can and should to mitigate risks.","ICT supply chain risks in electronic supply chains in China, DRC, India, Malaysia, Taiwan, and Thailand. Workers manufacturing electronic hardware.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below","Women
Migrants
Other vulnerable groups","temporary workers, agency workers","Congo (Democratic Republic)
China
India
Malaysia
Thailand
Taiwan","TfL is a member of Electronics Watch, and works with the organisation to address the human and labour rights risks in the ICT supply chains. Where risk are identified - Electronics Watch supports enforcement of our contract obligations. It worked to ensure good outcomes like a final assembly facility in India has no late payments of bonuses anymore and this did not recur. Also 158 Burmese Migrants were refunded for fees paid to secure their job. We use our leverage to aid this.",E-scooter batteries. Workers manufacturing in global supply chains with forced labour and labour rights risk.,Within your supply chains,"Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below","Women
Migrants
Other vulnerable groups","factory workers, agency workers",Taiwan,"Similar to issues with E-Bikes in previous statement, when sending out tenders - bidders have to provide us with evidence of their risk assessment to demonstrate Employer Pays Principle. This is apart of contract requirements for winning bidders.","Abuse of vulnerability
Withholding of wages
Abusive working and living conditions
Excessive overtime",No,"Financial remediation, including repayment of recruitment fees
Supporting victims via NGO",No,"We will strengthen our HRDD processes by creating a new ethical sourcing action plan template, addressing gaps identified through Electronics Watch, deepen supply chain mapping. We will update our risk assessment in 2026/27 and adjust the key suppliers list by including more risk factors, e.g. MSAT scores and supply chain mapping data. We will repeat MSAT campaign, providing training/follow ups to suppliers scoring below 70% and track progress through KPIs on supplier engagement and performance.",2026-10-13T16:08:25,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/EzzusHKG/2026/tfl-modern-slavery-statement-2025-26-signed.pdf
