Through trade unions or other worker representative groups",No,"We also adopt targeted measures to monitor working conditions, including regular human rights risk audits, issuance of the Supplier Code of Conduct and full-lifecycle supplier management systems.",No,"We surmise that potential human rights risks may exist within the production segment of photovoltaic module manufacturing, due to the application of manual labour.",Within your own operations,,Migrants,,China,"We respect and uphold the legal rights and interests of our employees and have established a comprehensive risk management system. We have also formulated a human rights due diligence mechanism spanning the entire business lifecycle, placing targeted focus on high-risk areas such as child labour and forced labour. Meanwhile, we conduct regular human rights risk audits and effectiveness evaluations of remedial measures to drive continuous improvement in management practices.","We surmise that potential labour employment risks may arise among the Group’s supporting suppliers, due to intricate multi-tiered supplier hierarchies.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below",Migrants,,China,"We have established an effective supply chain risk monitoring system, requiring suppliers to implement appropriate controls for their human rights risks and conducting comprehensive oversight of core suppliers. In 2025, we updated the Supplier Code of Conduct, which explicitly prohibits child labour, forced labour, employment discrimination and other misconduct, and mandates compliance with occupational health and safety standards.","We surmise that potential occupational health and workplace safety risks may be present across the Group’s supporting suppliers, due to intricate multi-tiered supplier hierarchies.",Within your supply chains,"Tier 2 suppliers
Tier 3 suppliers and below",Migrants,,China,"We have established an effective supply chain risk monitoring system, requiring suppliers to implement appropriate controls for their human rights risks and conducting comprehensive oversight of core suppliers. In 2025, we updated the Supplier Code of Conduct, which explicitly prohibits child labour, forced labour, employment discrimination and other misconduct, and mandates compliance with occupational health and safety standards.",,Yes,,,"We have outlined a series of forward-looking improvement measures, as detailed within the “Continued Improvement” section of this statement. It is our view that such measures will sustainably enhance the Company’s performance in mitigating human rights risks.",2026-06-26T07:03:05,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/cEWTcMDW/2026/Modern Slavery Statement (Longi Solar Technology Co Ltd).pdf
