India","Lutron manages this type of risk through its Third-Party Due Diligence Program, a multi-layered, risk-based program designed to identify, assess, and mitigate risks across its global supply chain.",,Yes,,,"Lutron’s Supplier Code of Conduct establishes expectations on human rights, labor practices, and ethical conduct. Our Conflict Minerals Statement addresses mineral sourcing risks. We provide periodic training to supply chain personnel on identifying forced labor, child labor, and human trafficking. Policies are periodically reviewed and updated. Third-party risk levels and issues are reported annually to Lutron’s Compliance & Risk Council and the Board’s Audit Committee.",2026-07-01T20:45:08,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/EFFj4gZT/2026/fy_2025_uk_anti-slavery_and_human_trafficking_position_statement.pdf
