Other vulnerable groups","Ex-offenders, homelessness persons",United Kingdom,"As before, we now have bespoke training to our frontline staff on identifying and spotting signs of modern slavery and how to report suspected incidents or anyone in immediate danger. The Combined Authority's Whistleblowing Protocol has been updated to now include references to Safeguarding and Modern Slavery. We have also maintained and updated our Modern Slavery Policy as mandatory reading for all members of staff.",Looking at our civic duty and the risks in our wider Liverpool City Region. Continue to partner with the Merseyside Police and Crime Commissioner as Vice Chair to the Modern Slavery Network.,Wider Liverpool City Region as a public sector body with a civic duty.,,"Women
Migrants
Refugees
Children
Other vulnerable groups",All residents of the Liverpool City Region,United Kingdom,"Continue to participate in existing Combined Authority partnerships focused on safeguarding, which includes modern slavery. We now Vice-Chair the Merseyside’s Police & Crime Commissioner Modern Slavery Network which brings together partners from across civic society to examine modern slavery in the City Region and to promote best practise in identification, prevention and mitigation; and put effective interventions in place to protect potential victims across the City Region.","Abuse of vulnerability
