Supporting investigations by relevant authorities",No,"We set KPIs on:
1)Number of collegues trained globally & regular meetings with Welfare sponsors who are 2nd level trained with regular check-ins
2)Transparancy on non-compliances open & closed & the classification of the root causes
We do not set KPIs on the number of cases we investigate - our policy is ""if we dont find any, we are not looking in the right places""  Success comes from reports in direct operations.  Our policy is Victim led -  we are unable to disclose some statistics.",2026-09-16T11:07:03,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/4C2u3sav/2026/Modern Slavery Report 2025-2026.pdf
