Refugees",,United Kingdom,Our Ethical Labour Policy for our Supply Chain is very clear on required compliance by our third parties including having effective controls to identify modern slavery in their own supply chains. One such example is the provision of appropriate training on modern slavery and ethical labour.,,Yes,,,"Our Statement includes a ‘Further Steps’ section to guide future efforts in tackling modern slavery and support continuous improvement. We are committed to an annual review of the Statement, providing a structured process for monitoring progress. The review incorporates input from senior leaders who are well placed to drive change within the business. These further steps are designed to deliver positive outcomes across several areas and with shared accountability for their implementation.",2026-08-10T09:43:30,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/dCz1asZH/2026/Modern Slavery Statement - FYE 30 Sep 2025.pdf
