Taiwan","Supplier partners must follow the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development Due Diligence Guidance and implement their 5-Step guidance. This risk-based approach is designed to help organisations avoid contributing to conflict, serious human rights impacts and financial crime through their operations. The framework includes embedding strong management systems, identifying risks, independent third-party audits and transparency.","Service providers we contract with present risks, for example, cleaning, construction, waste management, security, events and hospitality.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,"Women
Migrants
Refugees",,"United Kingdom
United States","The Group is committed the continuous assessment of our impact on human rights in our operations, taking prioritised action to mitigate risks and provide accessible grievance mechanisms for confidential reporting.  
As a result of our screening, service suppliers may be asked to undergo an audit and this is written into the terms of our Vendor Code of Conduct and explained within our Supplier Sustainability Standards.","There are internal risks linked to poor recruitment and management practices, lower skilled roles, insufficient pay, excessive working hours, poor working conditions and inadequate training.",Within your own operations,,"Women
Migrants",,"United Kingdom
United States",We maintain strong colleague engagement through a variety of interactive channels and implement financial initiatives to protect and support lower paid workers. We also provide information and training in relation to modern slavery and human rights issues and remind colleagues to be vigilant and report any suspected instances of wrongdoing in line with our Whistleblowing Policy.,,Yes,,,"Our Statement includes KPIs to improve transparency and 
