Workers within your organisation",No,,Yes,"Using anonymous whistleblowing services, such as a helpline or mobile phone app",No,"Screening and assessment of suppliers from human rights impacts, dedicated corrective action plans for suppliers that do not meet our expectations. None related to modern slavery or human trafficking.",Yes,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Yes,,,"The MAP2030 targets support our efforts, mainly under ‘responsible procurement’ and ‘human rights’. In 2025, we reviewed the Human Rights Due Diligence steps for all operations and defined actions where relevant. We continued our Responsible Procurement process by screening over 2,100 suppliers for sustainability risks, including human rights. We are transitioning to a continuous management approach where human rights are built into regular business processes.",2026-05-29T14:21:14,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/4nEEmdkB/2026/Mondi Modern Slavery Statement 2025.pdf
