Through trade unions or other worker representative groups",No,"We conduct audits for NMW, background checks and right to works and do so with agencies. Complete enhanced vendor DD and employee surveys. Circulate ethics compliance declarations for senior leaders.",Yes,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,Yes,,,"We have included details in our 2025 Statement on progress made on training, risk assessments, audits and supplier visits, updates to policy, enhanced vendor due diligence and strengthening governance for our customers in reducing the risk of modern slavery. We have reviewed and updated our vision & principles and began the process for establishing risk assessments. We intend to continue this momentum to work towards setting measurable Group-wide KPIs improving this further during 2026 and 2027.",2026-08-26T13:47:28,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/nsCV984i/2026/Modern Slavery Act 2026.pdf
