We learned we needed clearer ownership, stronger in‑life assurance and more targeted training and worker awareness. Next year we’ll take forward the recommendations to strengthen our approach.",,Yes,,,"Conducted 50 on-site supplier assessments to identify modern slavery risks. No concerns indicating potential forced labour identified via assessments or Speak Up. Achieved 98% completion of mandatory modern slavery training. Continued to support, fund and promote the UK Modern Slavery Helpline. Deployed a Worker Voice solution to five additional supply chain sites (~1,200 workers). Invested in the Child Rights Action Hub DRC to help address risk of child labour in our raw material supply chain.",2026-06-16T16:43:40,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/nERxCVAp/2026/BT_Modern-Slavery-Statement-June26.pdf
