Ukraine","Monjasa mitigates owned fleet risk through internal crew contracts, MLC compliance and onboard grievance mechanisms via the DPA and whistleblowing platform. HSEQ audits now include modern slavery checkpoints. Crew awareness e-learning is being integrated into Montec onboarding. ITF coverage gaps are being assessed, with two European vessels now covered by ITF agreements and one by national requirements.","Supply Chain
Supplier vessel crew present high inherent risk due to unknown working conditions and absent human rights policies. Key customers in high-risk jurisdictions also rated high risk.",Within your supply chains,Tier 1 suppliers,Other vulnerable groups,Crew working for chartered vessels under Flags that are not MLC ratified,Panama,"Monjasa embeds modern slavery checks into HSEQ vessel audits and applies risk criteria at chartering stage. Top suppliers and customers are screened, with high-risk counterparties engaged via the Code of Conduct. Targeted training was delivered to frontline staff with operational exposure, with e-learning being integrated into crew onboarding. Governance is underpinned by a board-approved Modern Slavery Statement, Human Rights Risk Register, Working Group, and open whistleblowing platform.",Office staff in conflict-affected regions and high-corruption countries such  face medium risk. Third-party service workers carry similar risk where labour protections remain unclear.,Within your own operations,,Other vulnerable groups,Workers working in countries with high prevalence of Modern Slavery and near conflict zones .,United Arab Emirates,"Monjasa uses direct contracts where possible, monitors legal compliance, and implements ISO 45001-aligned health and safety systems. A formal flexible working policy is being introduced for staff in conflict-affected offices, with whistleblowing awareness checks embedded into office audits.","Restriction of movement
