India","Third party audits at all tier one sites. Commissioned the specialist audit body TRN to conduct worker-focused, dialogue-based visits to selected factories based on risk. Training sessions and workshops for suppliers in our Chinese supply chain. All cotton sourced from China must be BCI certified. Restrictions on sourcing from countries and regions at extreme risk of human rights issues and/or where audits cannot be freely conducted.","Migrant worker exploitation in the fish
and seafood industry",Within your supply chains,Tier 2 suppliers,Migrants,,,"To address these risks within our supply chain we committed to funding and engaging in the ETI Shrimp responsible purchasing practices project. We are also developing a questionnaire to be directed to our key seafood suppliers to enhance our due diligence and identify potential actions to be taken in collaboration with our suppliers to improve working conditions in
our fish and seafood supply chain.",Abusive working and living conditions,No,Supporting investigations by relevant authorities,No,Our statement set goals and reports on progress in each case.,2026-05-01T14:34:07,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/CA1UjqsT/2026/Morrisons_MSR2025 .pdf
