Other vulnerable groups","agency or temporary workers, ethnic minority workers, contracted labour workers",China,"We have identified BYD bus manufacturing in China as a higher-risk supply chain area. To address this risk, suppliers are assessed through Sedex risk reviews and due diligence processes. Where available, independent third-party audit information is reviewed to assess labour standards and worker welfare. We engage with suppliers on any identified concerns and monitors corrective actions to support ethical employment practices and continuous improvement.",Temporary vehicle maintenance technicians recruited through labour agencies to carry out bus maintenance and refurbishment activities in the UK.,Within your own operations,,"Migrants
Other vulnerable groups",temporary and agency workers,United Kingdom,"We have identified the use of agency labour within vehicle maintenance and refurbishment activities as a higher-risk area. To address this risk, labour providers and suppliers are subject to due diligence and compliance checks. We monitor supplier performance, reviews employment practices and investigates any concerns raised. Where issues are identified, corrective actions are agreed and monitored to promote fair treatment, legal compliance and worker welfare.",,Yes,,,"Braddell Limited measures progress through supplier risk assessments, audit outcomes and corrective actions implemented. During the reporting period, the company continued to use the Sedex risk assessment framework, enhanced supplier due diligence and maintained whistleblowing channels for workers and suppliers. Looking ahead, Braddell has committed to enhancing employee training and continuing to strengthen its approach to identifying and managing modern slavery risks across its supply chain.",2026-05-06T09:37:30,https://downloads.modern-slavery-statement-registry.service.gov.uk/pdf-published/EkucCLVY/2026/Modern-Slavery-and-Human-Trafficking-Statement-2026.pdf
